{"title":"2019 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_(Detailed_Explanation)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 (Detailed Explanation)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2_by_Math-X_(First_fully_understand_the_problem)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2 by Math-X (First fully understand the problem)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_6_(CREATIVE_THINKING)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 6 (CREATIVE THINKING)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_7_by_The_Power_of_Logic(1_to_25_Full_Solution)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4.7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 7 by The Power of Logic(1 to 25 Full Solution)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is a rhombus with perimeter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/1/5e1d1611143f5792dc0f61f3b130af88cb790c04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$52$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> meters. The length of diagonal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> meters. What is the area in square meters of rhombus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/4/e54b35c6e9f6a1eaa16a3138ed06ebc73122be63.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((-13,0)--(0,5)); draw((0,5)--(13,0)); draw((13,0)--(0,-5)); draw((0,-5)--(-13,0)); dot((-13,0)); dot((0,5)); dot((13,0)); dot((0,-5)); label(&quot;A&quot;,(-13,0),W); label(&quot;B&quot;,(0,5),N); label(&quot;C&quot;,(13,0),E); label(&quot;D&quot;,(0,-5),S); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"125\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/3/e135c8466d2cc1949dec9fd2df70786ce686f5ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }60\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }90\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }105\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }120\\qquad\\textbf{(E) }144$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"426\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/0/230af487f6bb84b2940aef916f01294a89dfc2cf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((-12,0)--(0,5)); draw((0,5)--(12,0)); draw((12,0)--(0,-5)); draw((0,-5)--(-12,0)); draw((0,0)--(12,0)); draw((0,0)--(0,5)); draw((0,0)--(-12,0)); draw((0,0)--(0,-5)); dot((-12,0)); dot((0,5)); dot((12,0)); dot((0,-5)); label(&quot;A&quot;,(-12,0),W); label(&quot;B&quot;,(0,5),N); label(&quot;C&quot;,(12,0),E); label(&quot;D&quot;,(0,-5),S); label(&quot;E&quot;,(0,0),SW); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"132\" />\n</p><p>A rhombus has sides of equal length. Because the perimeter of the rhombus is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/1/5e1d1611143f5792dc0f61f3b130af88cb790c04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$52$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, each side is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/d/20d5cdacb8a4969dd1b57002a2e364d207478b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{52}{4}=13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"64\" height=\"38\" />. In a rhombus, diagonals are perpendicular and bisect each other, which means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/8/5e8bc36793a7c64d05fff20d519f0f72d9256fab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AE}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/7/07735d2b6021b01b9151420c69f0330ca0b544d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{EC}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Consider one of the\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/c/13cae96c6d58989310e8a27b3c7afe7ba5fc6c53.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((-12,0)--(0,5)); draw((0,0)--(-12,0)); draw((0,0)--(0,5)); dot((-12,0)); dot((0,5)); label(&quot;A&quot;,(-12,0),W); label(&quot;B&quot;,(0,5),N); label(&quot;E&quot;,(0,0),SE); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"132\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/8/5e8bc36793a7c64d05fff20d519f0f72d9256fab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AE}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Using the Pythagorean theorem, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/3/0f32db217d7630882c3441fa8821cd70a6958c3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BE}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\nYou know the Pythagorean triple, (5, 12, 13).\n</p><p>Thus the values of the two diagonals are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/4373e7b4be983c0315e82e1fda1df66ed34dd7fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BD}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\nThe area of a rhombus is = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/8/008a3c18dde2a506dd6d7f4074428dcd981f8ab5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{d_1\\cdot{d_2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"49\" height=\"37\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/e/d2ec622c3fa9aa6627c9016ab584bd79da3c1235.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{24\\cdot{10}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"51\" height=\"37\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/a/aaa4de95cc6371d125d5cf773cdd9f9913dd1d8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/0/760a948e3f1d763c40fef6f4baca7846a7f13036.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 120}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"74\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Right off the bat, we can see that the perimeter of the figure is 52. Dividing this by four, we can get that each side is equal to 13. By drawing a line perpendicular to the one given, we can split the figure into four right triangles. 12 (24/2) is equal to the height of one small right triangle, and 13 is the slanted side. Using the Pythagorean theorem we can find that 169 (13 squared) - 144 (12 squared) = 25 (five squared). With this, we can determine that each small right triangle equals 30. Multiplying that by four we can get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/0/760a948e3f1d763c40fef6f4baca7846a7f13036.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 120}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"74\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~math4all\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solutions\">Video Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span id=\"Video_Solution_1_.28Detailed_Explanation.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_(Detailed_Explanation)\">Video Solution 1 (Detailed Explanation)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 (Detailed Explanation)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/nbcPvG024_o\">https://youtu.be/nbcPvG024_o</a>\n</p><p>~ChillGuyDoesMath\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Video_Solution_2_by_Math-X_.28First_fully_understand_the_problem.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2_by_Math-X_(First_fully_understand_the_problem)\">Video Solution 2 by Math-X (First fully understand the problem)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2 by Math-X (First fully understand the problem)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/IgpayYB48C4?si=CGr1gRwXKdjrhl24&amp;t=678\">https://youtu.be/IgpayYB48C4?si=CGr1gRwXKdjrhl24&amp;t=678</a>\n</p><p>~Math-X\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_3\">Video Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The Learning Royal: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/IiFFDDITE6Q\">https://youtu.be/IiFFDDITE6Q</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_4\">Video Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-yHfOUapg7I&amp;list=PLbhMrFqoXXwmwbk2CWeYOYPRbGtmdPUhL&amp;index=5\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-yHfOUapg7I&amp;list=PLbhMrFqoXXwmwbk2CWeYOYPRbGtmdPUhL&amp;index=5</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_5\">Video Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/mL6gIb5y3B0\">https://youtu.be/mL6gIb5y3B0</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Video_Solution_6_.28CREATIVE_THINKING.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_6_(CREATIVE_THINKING)\">Video Solution 6 (CREATIVE THINKING)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 6 (CREATIVE THINKING)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/UCaEXbe7mN0\">https://youtu.be/UCaEXbe7mN0</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Video_Solution_7_by_The_Power_of_Logic.281_to_25_Full_Solution.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_7_by_The_Power_of_Logic(1_to_25_Full_Solution)\">Video Solution 7 by The Power of Logic(1 to 25 Full Solution)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 7 by The Power of Logic(1 to 25 Full Solution)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\